quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  8,26,"Remember when you were few (in Mecca), oppressed in the land, constantly fearing that the (powerful) people might snatch you away, then (after the migration to Medina) He sheltered you, strengthened you with His help and provided you with the good things so that you might be grateful."
  8,27,"O believers! Do not betray Allah and the Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him), and do not betray your trusts knowingly."
  8,28,Know that your possessions and your children are only a test (and temptation) and that Allah—with Him is an excellent reward.
  8,29,"O believers! If you become conscious of Allah, He will grant you a criterion (to distinguish between right and wrong), and He will absolve you of your misdeeds and forgive you. And Allah is the Lord of Mighty Grace."
  8,30,"And (remember) when the disbelievers were devising plans against you to confine you, or kill you, or expel you. They plotted, and Allah foiled their plots. And Allah is the Best of planners."
  8,31,"When Our revelations are recited to them, they say: ‘We have heard already. If we want, we (too) can say something similar. These are nothing but the (fictional) stories of the ancients.’"
  8,32,"And when they said: ‘O Allah! If this is the truth from You, rain down stones upon us from the sky, or bring us a painful punishment.’"
  8,33,"But (Esteemed Prophet!) Allah would never punish them while you are among them, nor would Allah punish them while they seek forgiveness."
